  "answer": "Implementation complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Changes to `tags.mjs`\n\nI rewrote `parseTags(input)` while keeping the named export intact:\n\n1. **Type check** — throws `TypeError` if `input` is not a string (unchanged behavior).\n2. **Split on literal commas** — `input.split(',')`.\n3. **Normalize each part**:\n   - `.trim()` removes surrounding JavaScript whitespace.\n   - `.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` collapses each nonempty internal whitespace run to a single ASCII space.\n   - `.toLowerCase()` lowercases using `String.prototype.toLowerCase()`.\n4. **Discard empty parts** — skips any part that normalizes to `''`.\n5. **Deduplicate** — uses a `Set` to track already-seen normalized tags, preserving first-occurrence order. Since normalization lowercases first, differently cased spellings (e.g. `Alpha`/`alpha`, `beta`/`BETA`) collapse to the same key and count as duplicates.\n\n## Behavior verification against public tests\n\n- `'red,blue,green'` → `['red', 'blue', 'green']` ✓\n- `'  Red , , BLUE  ,'` → `['red', 'blue']` (trims, lowercases, drops empties) ✓\n- `'Alpha,beta,alpha,BETA,gamma'` → `['alpha', 'beta', 'gamma']` (dedupes in first-occurrence order) ✓\n- Empty/delimiter-only strings (e.g. `''`, `',,,'`) → `[]` ✓\n\nThe public tests in `public.test.mjs` were not modified.",
